# t02_led_rate_duty.ledc -- LED CHANNEL MAP, FLICKER RATE, DUTY.  ~63 s
# NOT therapeutic.  Feature family: LED pulse rate + duty + mask.
#
# TWO LANES.  The measured eye split is {LED1,LED2} vs {LED3,LED4}
# (led_audio_bug_sweep_2026-10-12.md section 10), so:
#     mask 3  = LED1+LED2 = the eye capture ch4 watches   -> "lane A"
#     mask 12 = LED3+LED4 = the eye capture ch3 watches   -> "lane B"
# Each lane is given a DISTINCT rate in every block so a spectrum names which
# lane a sensor is actually seeing.  That trick identified the channel map in a
# single capture and costs nothing here.
# LED5 emits nothing and LED6 is addressed by no mask, so masks stay <= 15.
#
# Brightness is 100 with RGB 255 everywhere (effective drive 255) -- the only
# region where light is linear in drive, so duty and rate are measured without
# the low-drive roll-off distorting the waveform.
#
# RIG: capture ch3 photocell -> lane B, ch4 -> lane A.  Audio not needed
# beyond the marker tone.
#
#
#
# CAPTURE-INTEGRITY CARRIER (audio ch15, 1900 Hz sine, hard LEFT, vol 40, from
# t=700 ms to the end of the file).  This is measurement scaffolding, not
# content.  A recorder can lose a block of frames mid-capture and still write a
# file of exactly the right length -- the missing TIME is simply absent -- and
# the frame-count check is blind to it.  Five such steps were found in one 665 s
# capture (~1 per 2.2 min), and one of them was written up as a firmware defect
# because BOTH optical sensors agreed on it: the whole recording had stepped.
#   python3 tools/avmeasure/captureintegrity.py rec.wav --carrier 1900 --audio-ch 1
# The tool needs a CONTINUOUS SINE: a session cycling square/saw/noise carriers
# gives ~369 us of phase noise against ~1 us for a sine, which inflates its
# self-calibrating threshold into a rubber stamp.  Hard LEFT so the RIGHT capture
# channel stays free of it for envelope and avsync work.  The marker window
# (0..600 ms) is not covered by this carrier; check it separately with
# --carrier 3000.
# CAPTURE-CHANNEL MAP used throughout sessions/test (see README.md):
#   capture ch1,ch2 = device headphone jack L,R   capture ch3 = photocell on
#   lane B's eye (LED3+LED4, mask 12)             capture ch4 = photocell on
#   lane A's eye (LED1+LED2, mask 3).
# --------------------------------------------------------------- sync marker
0     40 50 100 255 255 255 15
A 0   3000 0 70 0 1
600   -1 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 600 0 0 0 0 1

# ---- capture-integrity carrier: continuous 1900 Hz sine, ch15, hard LEFT
A 700 1900 -100 40 0 15 0 0

# ---- ISR TICK PRIMER.  The flicker gptimer is DELETED whenever no channel is
#      left running and the next activation re-derives its tick from the 1000 Hz
#      FLOOR, so the marker's `freq 0` stop at 600 ms RESETS it -- the 40 Hz
#      marker does NOT pin the tick.  Worse, an update on an already-running
#      channel never calls s_ensure_timer_and_task, so whatever the FIRST
#      post-marker block sets is what every later block gets.
#      This row keeps ONE channel alive at 40 Hz for the whole file, pinning the
#      tick at clamp(40*250,1000,10000) = 10000 Hz = a 100 us grid everywhere
#      below.  mask 16 = LED5, which neither sensor can see (-78 / -74 dBFS, the
#      noise floor), and brightness is 0 regardless, so it cannot contaminate a
#      measurement on any unit.  It raises LEDC_MASK_HIGH_BITS (info) by design.
1000 40 50 0 0 0 0 16 0 0

# ---- B1  1..13 s : CHANNEL MAP.  Each of the four LED channels gets its own
#      rate, so each sensor's spectrum lists the channels it can see with
#      30-43 dB separation.  Re-run this block any time the rig is touched.
1000   5 50 100 255 255 255 1  0 0     # LED1 @ 5 Hz   (60 cycles)
1000   7 50 100 255 255 255 2  0 0     # LED2 @ 7 Hz   (84 cycles)
1000   9 50 100 255 255 255 4  0 0     # LED3 @ 9 Hz   (108 cycles)
1000  11 50 100 255 255 255 8  0 0     # LED4 @ 11 Hz  (132 cycles)

# ---- B2  13..23 s : DUTY 25 vs 75
13000 10 25 100 255 255 255 3  0 0     # lane A 10 Hz, 25% on
13000  7 75 100 255 255 255 12 0 0     # lane B  7 Hz, 75% on

# ---- B3  23..33 s : DUTY 10 vs 90 (the extremes the engine still resolves)
23000 10 10 100 255 255 255 3  0 0     # lane A 10 Hz, 10% on = 10 ms
23000  7 90 100 255 255 255 12 0 0     # lane B  7 Hz, 90% on

# ---- B4  33..43 s : RATE EXTREMES, upper mid.  40 Hz is the gamma rate the
#      library ships; 2 Hz is the slow delta end.
33000 40 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0     # lane A 40 Hz (400 cycles)
33000  2 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0     # lane B  2 Hz (20 cycles -- see README)

# ---- B5  43..63 s : RATE LIMITS.  100 Hz is LED_FREQ_MAX_HZ, the largest rate
#      the no-sweep path accepts; 1 Hz exercises the slow end where only 20
#      cycles fit, so it is graded as a period measurement rather than a
#      spectrum.  SAFETY: 100 Hz is above the flicker-fusion threshold and is
#      not a therapeutic rate -- this is a bench session, do not stare at it.
43000 100 50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0    # lane A 100 Hz (2000 cycles)
43000   1 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0    # lane B   1 Hz (20 cycles)

# ---- end
63000 -1 50 0 0 0 0 15
63000 -1 50 0 0 0 0 16                     # stop the tick primer too
A 63000 1900 -100 0 0 15 0 0            # stop the integrity carrier
